abstract:
Experiment E949 at Brookhaven National Laboratory has observed three new events consistent with the decay $K^+ 	o \pi^+ 
u  ar{
u}$ in the pion momentum region $140 < P_\pi < 199$ MeV/c in an exposure of $1.71 	imes 10^{12}$ stopped kaons with an estimated total background of $0.93 \pm 0.17^{+0.32}_{-0.24}$ events. This brings the total number of observed $K^+ 	o \pi^+ 
u  ar{
u}$ events to seven. Combining this observation with previous results, assuming the pion spectrum predicted by the standard model, results in a branching ratio of $(1.73^{+1.15}_{-1.05}) 	imes 10^{-10}$.
